[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{patterns}
\fill[gray!35] (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\begin{scope}
\clip (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\fill[white] (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\end{scope}
\draw (0,0) rectangle (8,4.6);
\draw (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\draw (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\node[anchor=north west, font=\small] at (0.15,4.5) {$\xi$};
\node at (1.9,4.15) {$D$};
\node at (6.1,4.15) {$K$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$D$ is the set of people who subscribe to Disney+ and $K$ is the set of people who subscribe to Kayo.
Which set describes the shaded region?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{patterns}
\fill[gray!35] (1.23,4.4) circle (0.8);
\begin{scope}
\clip (1.23,4.4) circle (0.8);
\fill[white] (2.17,4.4) circle (0.8);
\end{scope}
\draw (0,3.3) rectangle (3.4,5.8);
\draw (1.23,4.4) circle (0.8);
\draw (2.17,4.4) circle (0.8);
\node at (0.72,5.45) {$N$};
\node at (2.68,5.45) {$S$};
\node at (1.7,2.95) {$A$};
\fill[gray!35] (6.37,4.4) circle (0.8);
